Open Source License Attributions - Axon desktop

The following open-source components are used in the Axon desktop application.

This notice covers the native shell's Rust dependencies. The web bundle the
shell displays has its own notice, generated from the npm dependency tree and
readable inside the app under Settings -> Open-source licenses.

SYSTEM COMPONENTS

The application renders through the operating system's own web engine. These
are shared libraries provided by the platform rather than dependencies compiled
into this binary, so they do not appear in the crate list below and no tool
generates their attribution for us. They are recorded here deliberately.

  - WebKitGTK (Linux) - LGPL-2.1-or-later and BSD-style licences. Dynamically
    linked against the copy the distribution provides; the application neither
    bundles nor modifies it. Source: https://webkitgtk.org/
  - Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime (Windows) - proprietary, redistributable
    under the Microsoft Software License Terms for the WebView2 Runtime. Not
    bundled; the installer relies on the runtime present on the system.
  - WKWebView / WebKit (macOS) - supplied by the operating system as part of
    macOS. Apple's WebKit is available under LGPL-2.1 and BSD-style licences.
    Details: https://webkit.org/licensing-webkit/

